 markets:{title:'Markets & macro',topic:'Rates, risk & products',en:'What happens to the price of a fixed-rate bond when market yields rise, and why?',zh:'当市场收益率上升时，固定利率债券的价格会怎样变化？为什么？',guide:'Its price falls because future cash flows are discounted at a higher rate. Duration estimates sensitivity; convexity captures curvature.',retry:'Explain the intuition first, then distinguish duration, maturity, and coupon. State that other factors are held constant.'},
